# Z-Index Layers

## The Scale

```
z-pip      70   Picture-in-picture (minimized Jitsi call)
z-toast    60   Toast notifications, snackbars
z-modal    50   Modal/dialog content
z-overlay  40   Modal backdrop, dim overlay
z-dropdown 30   Dropdowns, context menus, popovers
z-float    20   Floating buttons (scroll-to-bottom, FAB)
z-sticky   10   Sticky headers, date separators
z-base      0   Default layer (everything else)
```

## Rules

### ALWAYS use semantic tokens

```tsx
// ✅ Semantic token
<div className="z-modal" />
<div className="z-dropdown" />
<div className="z-sticky" />

// ❌ NEVER hardcode numeric z-index
<div className="z-50" />
<div className="z-[999]" />
<div style={{ zIndex: 100 }} />
```

### Stacking order for overlapping UI

```
pip (70)       ← Jitsi minimized call (always on top)
  toast (60)   ← "Copied!", "Failed to send"
    modal (50) ← Edit dialog, Forward dialog, Search
      overlay (40) ← Dark backdrop behind modal
        dropdown (30) ← Context menu, emoji picker, instance switcher
          float (20) ← Scroll-to-bottom button
            sticky (10) ← Date header in message list
              base (0) ← Everything else
```

### Dropdown inside modal?

Radix UI handles this via Portals — dropdown renders in a portal at body level.
Both modal (50) and its inner dropdown (30) render at body level, so dropdown's z-30 < modal's z-50. 
If a dropdown must appear ABOVE a modal, render it as a Radix Portal with `z-modal`.

### Adding a new layer

If needed (rare), add to `tailwind.config.ts` → `theme.extend.zIndex`.
Never use `z-[arbitrary]` — add a named token instead.

## Token reference

Defined in `tailwind.config.ts`:

```typescript
zIndex: {
  base: "0",
  sticky: "10",
  float: "20",
  dropdown: "30",
  overlay: "40",
  modal: "50",
  toast: "60",
  pip: "70",
  max: "9999",  // emergency only — document why if used
}
```
